  "note": "First election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council under the 1922 wards, polled Monday 15 January 1923. The South Ward's five members were returned unopposed; the North Ward's seven seats were contested by eight candidates (Belfast News-Letter, 17 January 1923, p. 6). The nomination report (BNL 8 Jan 1923 p. 8) lists the four retiring Nationalists; the result report names the five returned unopposed as 'Daniel Lamont (Nat.), James A. M'Michael (Nat.), John Clarke (Nat.), Stephen Clarke (Nat.), and Peter Dallat (Nat.)' (image-read, BNL 17 Jan 1923 p. 6; Irish News 17 Jan 1923 p. 6 'Jas. A. M'Michael'), printed under 'North Ward' in error. Corrected from M'Alister (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
